At the Labour Party's campaign launch on 12 October 2008, Helen Clark became the latest world leader to guarantee bank deposits, unveiling a plan worth $150 billion whereby all retail deposits would be unconditionally covered.<ref name="stuff_deposits">{{cite web |url=http://www.stuff.co.nz/4725482a13.html |title=Govt deposit liability 'huge but risk low' |date=12 October 2008 |access-date=14 October 2008 |work=[[Stuff (website)|Stuff]] |location=New Zealand |archive-date=15 October 2008 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20081015103400/http://www.stuff.co.nz//4725482a13.html |url-status=live }}</ref> The plan would be voluntary to join; within two days, reports appeared stating that all of New Zealand's major trading banks had signed up.<ref name="stuff_deposits_b">
