|work=The Dominion Post |via=PressReader |location=New Zealand }}
</ref> Also signed up to the plan was the National Party, with deputy leader and finance spokesperson Bill English saying that there was "still time to change the...scheme if banks find it hard to borrow overseas".<ref name="rnz_deposit_timeto">
