== Results ==
The Labour government failed to secure a fourth consecutive term, after the National Party entered into support agreements with the ACT, United Future and Māori parties, resulting in a National minority government.<ref name="NBR_37836">{{cite news |url=http://www.nbr.co.nz/article/key-announces-shape-new-national-led-government-37836 |title=Key announces shape of new National-led government |date=16 November 2008 |agency=[[NZPA]] |work=[[National Business Review]] |access-date=30 October 2011 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131019130530/http://www.nbr.co.nz/article/key-announces-shape-new-national-led-government-37836 |archive-date=19 October 2013 }}</ref>

The Chief Electoral Officer released the official results on 22 November 2008.<ref>{{cite web|title=Results of the 2008 General Election|url=http://www.elections.org.nz/events/past-events-0/2008-general-election/results-2008-general-election|publisher=[[Electoral Commission (New Zealand)|Electoral Commission]]|access-date=17 April 2015|date=29 January 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150417231533/http://www.elections.org.nz/events/past-events-0/2008-general-election/results-2008-general-election|archive-date=17 April 2015}}</ref>

